	\subsection{The vertex types of degree 3}\label{deg3}

\subsubsection*{Case $\aaa\ccc^2$}

The AAD $\thin\aaa\thin\ccc^\bbb\thin^\bbb\ccc\thin$ of $\aaa\ccc^2$ gives $\thin\bbb\thin\bbb\thin\cdots$. Similar to the proof of Lemma \ref{deg345}, $\bbb^2\cdots$ can never be a vertex.
	


