When $\thin\bbb_3\thin\aaa_2\thin\aaa\thin\cdots$ appears, $\thin\bbb_3\thin\aaa_2\thin\aaa\thin\cdots=\thin\bbb_3\thin\aaa_2\thin\aaa\thin\ccc\thin\cdots$ determines $T_4,T_5$ in the first; $\thin\bbb_5\thin\aaa_4\thin\cdots=\thin\bbb_5\thin\aaa_4\thin\aaa\thin\ccc\thin\cdots$ determines $T_6,T_7$. Similarly, $T_8,T_9$ are determined but $\aaa^5\cdots$ appears, contradicting the AVC. 

When $\thin\bbb_3\thin\aaa_2\thin\ccc\thin\cdots$ appears, $T_4$ is determined in the second. Then $\thin\bbb_4\thin\aaa_2\thin\aaa_1\thin\cdots=\aaa^2\bbb\ccc^j$ determines $T_5,T_6$; $\bbb^2\cdots=\bbb^2\ccc$ determuines $T_7$. Since $\thin\aaa_2\thin\aaa_1\thin\ccc_5\thin\cdots$ appears, $\thin\bbb_5\thin\aaa_1\thin\cdots=\thin\bbb_5\thin\aaa_1\thin\ccc\thin\cdots=\thin\ccc\thin\aaa\thin\bbb_5\thin\aaa_1\thin\ccc\thin\cdots$ determines $T_8,T_9,T_{10}$. Similarly, we can determine $T_{11},T_{12},T_{13}$ but $\aaa\bbb^2\cdots$ appears, contradicting the AVC.

